      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Some additional observations:\n- avatar creators should not retain the ability to update a public fallback at any time; instead VRChat should control a \"branch\" of the package that, maybe, can get updated from the main branch when needed",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-08-30T21:19:28.113Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The current set of avatars available publicly for use as fallbacks is way too small, and almost all of them are woefully maladapted for people's avatar needs.\nUltimately an automated system for creating public avatars would be great. See: https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/implement-avatar-labs-system-for-public-fallbacks\nPlease don't make us wait until the developer time is available to implement that system. In the interim please establish a formal, limited, small-scale, human-driven process by which avatar creators can submit their avatar for public use as fallbacks, and listing in the browser.",
